:: Robin Chocolate Kiss
<<effects>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<person1>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"M-Maybe I can distract you," you say, moving closer to Robin.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
	"I can think of a better way to wait," you say, shifting closer beside <<him>>.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
	"I refuse to spend all this time hiding from snowballs," you say. "Come here."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Can I stay close?" you ask, moving beside Robin.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"I know what we can do while we wait," you say, kneeling beside Robin and placing a hand on <<his>> shoulder.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	"Forget them," you say, gripping the front of Robin's coat and pulling <<him>> closer. "They can waste their time."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Come here," you say, moving closer until your knee touches <<his>> leg.
<<else>>
	"I know how we can pass the time," you say, crawling on top of Robin.
<</if>>

<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	Robin gives a small nod. You rest a hand on <<his>> shoulder and kiss <<his>> neck.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "neutral")>>
	You rest a hand on Robin's shoulder, lean in, and kiss <<his>> neck.
<<else>>
	You lean over Robin and kiss <<his>> neck.
<</if>>
<<He>> laughs at first, then draws a quick breath as you kiss <<him>> again.
<br><br>

<<if _robin.trauma gte 40>>
	Robin keeps both arms around you instead of kissing back very much. You slow down, then settle beside <<him>> with your arms around <<his>> waist.
	<<npcincr Robin trauma -2>><<lrtrauma>>
<<else>>
	Robin returns the kisses, keeping one arm around you while you remain hidden behind the stand.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<generate2>>
After a while, the delinquents stop throwing snowballs and leave. You are still close to Robin when a voice calls from the other side of the stand. "Hello?" a <<person2>><<personsimple>> says. "The hot chocolate smells good. Is anyone around?"
<br><br>

<<person1>>
You move away from Robin so <<he>> can stand. The customer blinks when <<he>> suddenly appears from behind the counter, while you stay out of sight.
<<if _robin.trauma lt 40>>
	<<person2>><<He>> would quickly realise you and Robin were making out if <<he>> saw you both.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinChocolateOfferHelp>>

:: Hot Chocolate Doren
<<effects>>
<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<pass 60>><<famegood 1>>
<<person2>>
<<speechresolve>>

<<if $phase is 1>> /* offer to pay */
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"M-Maybe I can pay for them instead?" you ask.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"If it helps, I can pay for them," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I can pay for them," you say. "You don't need to keep arguing."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"Fine. I'll pay for them, then," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		"Stop arguing. I'll pay for them," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"I'll cover it," you say, reaching for your money.
	<<else>>
		"I can pay for them," you suggest.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	"No," Doren and Robin say at the same time.
	<br><br>

	Doren keeps arguing that <<he>> can afford it and wants to pay. Robin finally gives in and nods.
<<elseif $phase is 2>> /* convince Robin */
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"Doren's right," you say. "You need the money too, Robin. You should let <<him>> pay."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"Doren's right, Robin," you say. "You're helping by making the drinks, but you still have to pay for the milk and cocoa."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"Please take it, Robin," you say. "Doren wants to pay, and you need the money."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"Robin, stop trying to give everything away," you say. "You need the money too."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		"Take the money, Robin," you say. "You can't keep buying supplies if you give everything away."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"Take it, Robin," you say. "Doren can afford it, and you need the money."
	<<else>>
		"Doren's right, Robin," you say. "You need the money yourself."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	Doren agrees with you and pushes the money back across the counter. Robin looks between the two of you before finally nodding.
<<else>> /* support Robin's point */
	<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		"W-We can't take your money if you're giving these away," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "polite">>
		"Robin's right," you say. "If these are for people who need them, let us help too."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
		"Robin's right," you say. "You're handling the giving. Let us handle the drinks."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"Robin wants to help," you say. "Please let <<him>>."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"No," you say. "If you're giving them away for free, so are we."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		"Keep your money," you say. "We're not charging you for feeding people."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"Robin's right," you say. "We're not taking it."
	<<else>>
		"Robin's right. We can't take money from you for this," you say.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	Doren refuses to leave without paying. <<He>> pushes the money back towards Robin until Robin finally gives in and nods.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _robin.trauma gte 40>>
	"Okay, if you say so..." Robin says.
<<else>>
	"All right. Let's do this!" Robin says.
<</if>>
<br><br>

Robin sets another pot of milk on the stove. You line cups across the counter while Doren measures out cocoa and sugar. Robin fills the cups one by one, and Doren packs them into <<person2>><<his>> bag as soon as they are ready.
<br><br>

"Thanks a lot, you two!" Doren says. <<He>> hands Robin £$dorenhotchocoprice, closes <<his>> bag, then waves before walking away.
<br><br>
<<set $robinmoney += $dorenhotchocoprice>>
<<unset $dorenhotchocoprice>><<unset $dorenhotchocoamount>>
<<robinChocolateOfferHelp>>
